<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρμηξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηκος</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρμαξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱκος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Frr.</u>
				14.5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				76.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				9.31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.107
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦται θαλάσσης μύρμηκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschrio
					2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρμηκος ἀτραποί,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρμηκιά</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				100
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> fabulous
			animal in India, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.102
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ χρυσωρύχοι μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.1.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέουσι τοῖς καλουμένοις μύρμηξιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					16.4.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				69
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>hidden rock</i> in the sea, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				878
			</span></i>; esp. on the Thessalian coast between Sciathus and Magnesia,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.183
			</span></i>; off Smyrna, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				5.119
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> a sort
			of <i>gauntlet</i> or <i>cestus</i> with metal studs or nails
				<i>like warts</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρμηκίαι</span>) on
			it, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.150
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόρμαξ, ὅρμικας</span>,
				Skt.<i>vamrás</i>,
			Avest.<i>maoiriš</i>, OIr.<i>moirb</i>, OSlav.
				<i>mrav[icaron]ji</i>, ONorse <i>maurr</i>, Engl.
				(<i>pis-)mire</i>, Lat.<i>formica</i>: I.-<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> forms perh. <i>momro-, momrīˇ-,
			memro</i>- 'ant'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
